body:
I unfortunately don't have a reproducible example either, however I'm also seeing increases in rebuilds in our production application. I have a 2.4 -> 3.2 upgrade staged and I'm seeing the following change in times:

Activity | 2.4 | 3.2
--------|-----|---
Prod build (e.g. full optimizations, minify) | 111.47s | **96.75s**
Local dev builds (e.g. watch mode, hot module, no minify) | 88.28s | **66.84s**
Partial rebuild (comment out random import, then uncomment) | **5.16s** | 8.32s

Commenting this to add additional reports of this behavior. (I have the latest 3.2.0 that was released yesterday).

The only changes I made were upgrading the following npm packages: 

- `webpack` 2.4.1 -> 3.2.0.
- `webpack-dev-server` 2.4.5 -> 2.5.1
- `eslint-loader` 1.7.1 -> 1.9.0
- `babel-core` 6.24.1 -> 6.25.0
- `babel-eslint` 7.2.1 -> 7.2.3
- `babel-loader` 7.0.0 -> 7.1.1

And our vendors module as configured is aggressive about only containing code from `node_modules` to ensure infrequently changing vendors bundles (none of this was changed in the upgrade):

```javascript
//...
        new webpack.IgnorePlugin(/pdfjs\.worker/, /node_modules\/pdfjs-dist/),
        new webpack.ContextReplacementPlugin(/moment[\/\\]locale$/, /en/),
//...
        new webpack.optimize.CommonsChunkPlugin({
            name: 'vendors',
            minChunks: module => {
                return module.context 
                    && module.context.indexOf('node_modules') !== -1
                    //Deliberately ignore anything to do with pdf.worker in the vendor bundle
                    && (!module.resource || module.resource.indexOf('pdf.worker') === -1);
            }
        }),
//...
        new webpack.optimize.CommonsChunkPlugin({
            name: 'manifest',
            minChunks: Infinity
        }),
```
